<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECHS WORRIED BY BUSINESS, HAPPY WITH HAVEL- POLL.</title>
<headline>CZECHS WORRIED BY BUSINESS, HAPPY WITH HAVEL- POLL.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czechs are generally critical</p>
<p>about their country's social and political climate and are</p>
<p>especially disatisfied with current economic developments,</p>
<p>an opinion poll obtained by Reuters on Tuesday said.</p>
<p>The poll by the independent Centre for Empirical Research</p>
<p>(STEM), which was conducted at the beginning of January among</p>
<p>1,617 Czechs, showed a worsening of attitudes towards</p>
<p>privatisation and economic reform but gave the thumbs up to</p>
<p>President Vaclav Havel and the state of Czech democracy.</p>
<p>Respondents were asked to evaluate a range of different</p>
<p>spheres of public life and to rate their opinions in a one to</p>
<p>five range where one meant &quot;absolutely satisfied&quot; and five</p>
<p>&quot;absolutely dissatisfied&quot;.</p>
<p>The results, which average out the total responses, are</p>
<p>compared with a similar poll conducted in January 1995.</p>
<p>							   1997	    1995</p>
<p> president's work				    2.01	    2.40</p>
<p> possibility to use one's abilities	    2.49	    2.61</p>
<p> guarantee of civic freedom			2.61	    2.72</p>
<p> development of democracy			  2.71	    2.80</p>
<p> government's work				   2.98	    2.86</p>
<p> perspectives for future			   3.00	    3.03</p>
<p> party political system			    3.01	    3.05</p>
<p> work of local administration		    3.09	    2.98</p>
<p> political situation in the country	    3.22	    2.98</p>
<p> economic reform				     3.25	    2.94</p>
<p> work of parliament				  3.39	    3.47</p>
<p> social policy					 3.51	    3.57</p>
<p> results of privatisation			  3.60	    3.16</p>
<p> honesty in personal relations		   3.60	    3.63</p>
<p> honesty in business				 3.80	    3.98</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
